    {
      "course_code": "ENVE",
      "course_num": "401",
      "course_combined": "ENVE 401",
      "title": "Intro Water Resources Eng",
      "catalog_entry_url": "https://ssb.iit.edu/bnrprd/bwckctlg.p_disp_course_detail?cat_term_in=202710&subj_code_in=ENVE&crse_numb_in=401",
      "course_description": "The theory and practice involved in planning and design of water systems are introduced in this course. Topics include hydraulics, hydrology, storm water management, water supply distribution, and waste water collection and transport systems. Hydraulics includes flow of fluids through orifices, weirs, venturi meters, laminar and turbulent flow in closed conduits, open channel flow. Hydrology includes rainfall, runoff, and collection and distribution of water. Model analysis using the principles of dimensional analysis and software applications.",
